WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.163 --> 00:00:05.649
- [Voiceover] The
fundamental basis of life

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:09.739
comes down to this: the
struggle between good and evil,

00:00:09.739 --> 00:00:12.822
the fight between light and darkness.

00:00:14.899 --> 00:00:18.777
But in the DC universe,
things are not quite so clear.

00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:20.777
Heroes are sometimes complicated

00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:24.440
and villains are always complicated.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.953
- Hi boys.

00:00:25.953 --> 00:00:27.212
- [Voiceover] When it
comes to antiheroes,

00:00:27.212 --> 00:00:29.712
no one tops the Suicide Squad.

00:00:30.782 --> 00:00:34.112
The original Suicide Squad
first showed up in 1959.

00:00:34.112 --> 00:00:36.412
Though it disappeared
until being resurrected

00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:40.617
in its modern version in
1987, in the Legend series.

00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:42.489
The squad is comprised of the world's most

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:43.948
dangerous criminals who are on something

00:00:43.948 --> 00:00:45.997
of a work release program.

00:00:45.997 --> 00:00:47.848
Assembled by government
operative Amanda Waller,

00:00:47.848 --> 00:00:49.856
they are tasked with black-ops missions,

00:00:49.856 --> 00:00:52.118
in exchange for a chance
to earn their freedom.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.270
- Let's go save the world.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.704
- That's a good idea, honey.

00:00:54.704 --> 00:00:56.822
- [Voiceover] Through the
years, the squad has had

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:59.745
a revolving cast of characters,
with a few mainstays.

00:00:59.745 --> 00:01:01.844
The crew assembled in David Ayer's take,

00:01:01.844 --> 00:01:03.862
stemmed from the 2011 reboot of the comic.

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:06.659
There's Captain Boomerang, El Diablo,

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:10.576
Killer Croc, Enchantress,
Slipknot, and Katana.

00:01:12.041 --> 00:01:15.119
With a few of them making
their live action debut.

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:16.607
And then there's this guy.

00:01:16.607 --> 00:01:18.492
That's Deadshot, aka Floyd Lawton,

00:01:18.492 --> 00:01:20.220
as he's known in the civilian world.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.938
Obviously played here by Will Smith.

00:01:21.938 --> 00:01:25.069
Deadshot showed up in
Gotham as early as 1950,

00:01:25.069 --> 00:01:26.690
where he claimed to be a crime fighter,

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.206
before he emerges as Batman's enemy.

00:01:29.206 --> 00:01:31.190
Here's the original, fancy Deadshot,

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.021
who looks like a cross between
the Penguin and the Joker.

00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:36.435
His updated costume usually
includes an eye scope,

00:01:36.435 --> 00:01:38.935
a mask and wrist mounted guns.

00:01:39.848 --> 00:01:41.703
That's Harley Quinn,
one of the most popular

00:01:41.703 --> 00:01:44.285
of all female comic characters.

00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:47.420
- Seriously, the hell's
wrong with you people?

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.835
- We're bad guys, it's what we do.

00:01:50.835 --> 00:01:52.432
- [Voiceover] The former Arkham
psychiatrist who went crazy

00:01:52.432 --> 00:01:54.124
after falling in love with the Joker,

00:01:54.124 --> 00:01:56.246
didn't actually make her debut in a comic,

00:01:56.246 --> 00:01:58.897
but in Batman, the Animated Series.

00:01:58.897 --> 00:02:00.874
Artist Paul Dini got the
inspiration for Quinn

00:02:00.874 --> 00:02:03.015
while watching the soap
opera, Days of Our Lives,

00:02:03.015 --> 00:02:04.456
where his friend Arleen Sorkin

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:07.088
was playing a clown in a dream sequence.

00:02:07.088 --> 00:02:09.008
David Ayer maintained Quinn's iconography,

00:02:09.008 --> 00:02:10.823
but updated it, giving Margot Robbie

00:02:10.823 --> 00:02:12.924
a playful, but deviant look.

00:02:12.924 --> 00:02:17.007
And what would Harley
Quinn be without the Joker?

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.659
Ayer's Joker, played by Jared Leto,

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:22.888
is tatted out and styled after drug lords

00:02:22.888 --> 00:02:24.804
that Ayer saw on Instagram.

00:02:24.804 --> 00:02:26.363
Controversial?

00:02:26.363 --> 00:02:28.862
Maybe, but apparently
the tattoos tell part

00:02:28.862 --> 00:02:30.318
of Joker's backstory.

00:02:30.318 --> 00:02:33.781
- I can't wait to show you my toys.

00:02:33.781 --> 00:02:35.214
- [Voiceover] Indeed,
Suicide Squad might be our

00:02:35.214 --> 00:02:37.099
first chance to really explore

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:39.437
some of our favorite characters’ stories.

00:02:39.437 --> 00:02:43.270
The time has come for
the bad guys to shine. `

